  {
    "name": "warp_affine",
    "python": "warp_affine",
    "visibility": "public",
    "doc": "Apply a 2x3 affine transformation matrix.\n\nThe matrix ``[a, b, tx, c, d, ty]`` is a **forward** mapping from\nsource to destination (same convention as OpenCV ``warpAffine``)::\n\n    x_dst = a * x_src + b * y_src + tx\n    y_dst = c * x_src + d * y_src + ty\n\nThe kernel inverts this matrix internally for interpolation.\n\nDomain: buffer → buffer\n\nExample:\n    ```python\n    >>> # Translate image by (50, 30)\n    >>> pipe = Pipeline().source(\"image_bytes\").warp_affine(\n    ...     matrix=[1.0, 0.0, 50.0, 0.0, 1.0, 30.0],\n    ...     output_size=(224, 224),\n    ... )\n    >>>\n    >>> # Per-sample random affine: each row uses its own matrix columns\n    >>> pipe = Pipeline().source(\"image_bytes\").warp_affine(\n    ...     matrix=[pl.col(\"a\"), pl.col(\"b\"), pl.col(\"tx\"),\n    ...             pl.col(\"c\"), pl.col(\"d\"), pl.col(\"ty\")],\n    ...     output_size=(224, 224),\n    ... )\n    ```",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "matrix",
        "doc": "Six-element sequence representing the 2x3 affine matrix\n``[a, b, tx, c, d, ty]`` (forward mapping). **Each element may be a\nliteral float or a Polars expression**, so a batch can apply a\ndifferent (e.g. random) affine per row in one call — the matrix is\nresolved per row at execution.",
        "positional": true,
        "type": {
          "kind": "array",
          "len": 6,
          "inner": {
            "kind": "scalar",
            "per_row": true,
            "py": "float"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "output_size",
        "doc": "``(height, width)`` of the output image. Each element accepts a Polars\nexpression for per-row dynamic values.",
        "positional": true,
        "type": {
          "kind": "array",
          "len": 2,
          "inner": {
            "kind": "scalar",
            "per_row": true,
            "py": "int"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "interpolation",
        "doc": "Interpolation method -- ``\"bilinear\"`` (default) or ``\"nearest\"``.",
        "positional": false,
        "default": "bilinear",
        "type": {
          "kind": "scalar",
          "per_row": true,
          "py": "InterpolationType",
          "variants": [
            "nearest",
            "bilinear"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "border_value",
        "doc": "Pixel value for out-of-bounds regions (default 0).",
        "positional": false,
        "default": 0.0,
        "type": {
          "kind": "scalar",
          "per_row": true,
          "py": "float"
        }
      }
    ]
